    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math learning by adapting to individual paces and styles. For example, they can provide step-by-step solutions for problems, explain concepts in simple language, and generate practice exercises. This helps students overcome gaps in understanding without overwhelming them with theory."
